WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:13.969
Hey youtubers, It’s charlie, welcome to
part 2 of my many part game of thrones season

00:00:13.969 --> 00:00:14.969
4 preview.

00:00:14.969 --> 00:00:17.930
I’d like to say it’s going to be three
parts, but I could talk all year about a song

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:20.740
of ice and fire, so we’ll see.

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:23.840
In case you didn’t see my part 1 video I’m
separating each of these previews by geographic

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:26.000
region relatively.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.130
A lot of people wander.

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:31.820
This video will cover all the characters in
the north and around the wall including Arya

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:33.810
who is said wanderer.

00:00:33.810 --> 00:00:37.460
There will be some spoilers, but I’ll try
to warn you before in case you want to just

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:38.530
mute the audio for a sec.

00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:41.264
In which case you’ll have to wait till next
January to find out what’s going on, so

00:00:41.264 --> 00:00:45.780
I would advise watching the whole video so
we can geek out on Game of Thrones together.

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:47.300
It’s way more fun with other people.

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:48.300
Shall we begin!

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:50.469
So let’s start with the starks, primarily
Jon Snow.

00:00:50.469 --> 00:00:58.960
If you look carefully, you’ll see in the
opening credits Kit Harington is actually

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:05.560
featured as one of the bigger main cast members.

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:13.080
He is a major character in the books, but
I feel like the show gives some actors more

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:15.660
lines and scenes based on who the producers
consider to be the most important.

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:22.390
And if season 3 was big for Jon Snow, then
season 4 will be so much bigger.

00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:26.030
Remember that after the finale he had just
made it back to the night’s watch after

00:01:26.030 --> 00:01:30.750
going through what I’m calling a pretty
normal ‘wildling breakup’.

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:36.920
Think of that conversation, look man I either
we talk all night about our relationship and

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:43.650
were we’re going as a couple, or I can shoot
you with three arrows....Thinks about it for

00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:46.730
a minute...I’ll take the arrows.

00:01:46.730 --> 00:01:48.790
That Jon Snow, not much for small talk.

00:01:48.790 --> 00:01:51.030
Here’s where we start to get into spoiler
territory.

00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:54.840
I’ll try to be as vague as possible for
anyone who likes to find out via internet

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:57.780
sleuthing or reading the books.

00:01:57.780 --> 00:02:02.440
Jon Snow doesn’t move around much as a character,
not nearly as much as Arya, so he’s going

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:08.149
to be spending all of season 4 back with the
Night’s Watch.

00:02:08.149 --> 00:02:12.170
There aren’t going to be a lot of new characters
at the Wall.

00:02:12.170 --> 00:02:18.960
We’ll see one character from season 2 come
back, his name is Janos Slynt and he was the

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:25.060
person Tyrion fired as head of the gold cloaks
in kings landing before the battle of blackwater

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:26.060
bay.

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:29.320
Remember he made Bronn the leader of the gold
cloaks before Tywin came back at the end of

00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:30.320
that season.

00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:33.520
Since nobody knew about Jon’s secret mission
to infiltrate the wildlings you can imagine

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:36.470
the shit he’s going to be taking since everyone
thinks he was a traitor.

00:02:36.470 --> 00:02:40.710
I won’t say specifically what happens, but
the night’s watch itself goes through some

00:02:40.710 --> 00:02:43.510
changes just as a big battle is coming.

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:45.970
Which leads me back to the wildlings.

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:48.740
Remember they were in the middle of their
march on the night’s watch.

00:02:48.740 --> 00:02:50.820
There’s actually a new character called
The Magnar of thenn.

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:57.150
He’s just another general in the wildling
army like Tormund Giant’s Bane.

00:02:57.150 --> 00:03:01.190
The producers actually gave a lot of the book
scenes the magnar had to tormund in season

00:03:01.190 --> 00:03:04.120
3 to cut down on the number of new cast members.

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:05.120
That problem is only going to get worse, they’ve
already cut out a lot of subplots from the

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:08.130
first half of book 3, now that we’re moving
into the second part and parts of book 4,

00:03:08.130 --> 00:03:11.160
we’re going to see fewer and fewer book
characters.

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:14.620
That’s not necessarily a bad thing, but
for anyone keeping track, let’s just say

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:19.590
we’ll only be getting two or three battles
if that, and that includes Dany in Mereen.

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:22.730
I’ll talk about her in another preview video,
but let’s talk about Arya.

00:03:22.730 --> 00:03:24.852
She was one of my favorite characters in season
3.

00:03:24.852 --> 00:03:25.852
Arya spends most of her time wandering, but
because the show moves so quickly I think

00:03:25.852 --> 00:03:26.852
we’ll get some really good arya action in
the first two episodes.

00:03:26.852 --> 00:03:30.650
Think of Arya and the hound in the first couple
of episodes as being like a little sister

00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:31.650
and a big daddy from bioshock.

00:03:31.650 --> 00:03:33.770
You want to stay as far away from them as
possible.

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:35.390
Her other nickname now is stabby mcgee.

00:03:35.390 --> 00:03:36.390
(stabbing motion).

00:03:36.390 --> 00:03:43.550
If you remember the shot of arya with her
valar morghulis coin, that storyline will

00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:48.130
move forward and I think we’ll get to see
her use it near the end of the season.

00:03:48.130 --> 00:03:49.300
Definitely before episode 9.

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:53.010
Someone in the comments asked me about her
valyrian steel blade Needle, she does get

00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:54.010
it back.

00:03:54.010 --> 00:03:55.870
I won’t say how, but it’s going to be
awesome.

00:03:55.870 --> 00:03:59.130
Don’t you just feel like her scenes make
you want to laugh, but because they’re so

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:02.190
dark or she’s so nuts you feel awful every
time you do.

00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:10.740
I think it’s just because she looks so young,
it’s so unexpected to see such a little

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:16.380
girl act the way she does and speak with so
much conviction.

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:18.100
In the books she’s supposed to be about
13 years old.

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:22.090
Ygritte is still a part of the story, you
remember she had that heartbreaking scene

00:04:22.090 --> 00:04:26.760
with Jon Snow at the end of season 3.

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:29.330
Remember what she said to him before they
climbed the wall.

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:31.220
“Don’t ever betray me...”

00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:35.800
Let me know in the comments what you think
she’s going to do when she sees Jon Snow

00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:36.800
again.

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:39.620
Let’s just say it’s not like running into
your ex-girlfriend in a movie theater.

00:04:39.620 --> 00:04:40.740
waaay more awkward.

00:04:40.740 --> 00:04:43.540
Those wildling women, gotta be careful, yikes.

00:04:43.540 --> 00:04:48.060
I’m going to save any of the other supporting
characters for another video, but send me

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:50.440
